{
	"source": "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1LQP237JEehyA3XaCPb0CpCdvS5BMl86wqPHdSFcV5xY (PrUn community ship repair / damage calculator by RNGzero, credits: PrUn Community Tools Discord, lowstrife, Archiel, AEM, neke86)",
	"retrieved": "2026-08-09",
	"description": "Transcribed from the community sheet's own cells and formulas. Two things live here: the REPAIR BILL law (how many of each component a repair at a given damage consumes) and the DAMAGE TYPE split (every trip's damage divided into wear, meteoroid, heat and radiation, each reducible by its own shield). Component PRICES are deliberately not carried: PRUNplanner already prices tickers from the API, so the sheet's ci figures are recorded only as the snapshot that let us verify the law.",
	"repairBill": {
		"formula": "count = ceil(componentCount x damageFraction x 0.75 x factor), where factor is `shieldRelief` for the hull plate and structural elements and 0.662 for each shield; plus a flat MFK 12 and FLP 8 whatever the ship and the damage. shieldRelief = 1 - sum(relief of every installed shield).",
		"hullShare": 0.75,
		"shieldShare": 0.662,
		"shieldRelief": {
			"BPT": 0.05,
			"BWH": 0.05,
			"BRP": 0.05,
			"APT": 0.15,
			"AWH": 0.15,
			"ARP": 0.1,
			"SRP": 0.15
		},
		"fixed": {
			"MFK": 12,
			"FLP": 8
		},
		"verified": "A 90 plate LHP ship at 20% damage: ceil(90 x .2 x .75) = 14 plates, and 14x4000 + 12x180 + 8x400 = 61,360 ci, the sheet's own figure. The fully shielded AHP ship reproduces at 253,860 ci.",
